### Panda Pocket - Settlement, the ZAR ledger and webhook delivery
###
### Settlement owns the merchant's rand balance, the platform's fee income, and
### delivery of signed notifications to merchant servers.
###
### The three call types in this system get three different resilience
### strategies, and the difference is the point rather than an accident:
###
###   Invoice -> Rate       critical path, must not block. Circuit breaker with
###                         a cached fallback. Better a slightly stale rate than
###                         a checkout that hangs. (day 6)
###   Invoice -> Settlement it is money, and must not be lost. Retry, backed by
###                         an idempotent endpoint so retrying is safe, plus a
###                         sweeper for anything the inline retries miss.
###   Settlement -> merchant external and untrusted. Durable queue, exponential
###                         backoff with jitter, and dead-lettering.

@gw = http://localhost:5000
@settlement = http://localhost:5004
@key = pk_live_demo0000000000000000000000000000000000
@merchantId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### The ledger
###
### Settling one R250 invoice writes TWO entries, not one net entry:
###
###   Credit  +250.00   balance 250.00
###   Fee       -2.50   balance 247.50
###
### "You were paid R250 and we took R2.50" is a statement a merchant can check.
### A single R247.50 line hides where the difference went, and makes platform fee
### income impossible to sum. The amounts are signed so the balance is a plain
### SUM of the column rather than a conditional that has to know which types
### subtract.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{gw}}/api/settlements/{{merchantId}}/ledger?pageSize=10
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Current position.
GET {{gw}}/api/settlements/{{merchantId}}/balance
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Reconciliation.
###
### merchant_balances is a CACHE of ledger_entries: everything in it is
### derivable by summing the entries, and it exists only so that showing a
### balance is one row read instead of an aggregate over the merchant's whole
### history. This endpoint recomputes the sum and compares, which is what proves
### the cache has not drifted. A mismatch raises a CRITICAL security event.
GET {{gw}}/api/settlements/{{merchantId}}/reconcile
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Another merchant's ledger. 403.
GET {{gw}}/api/settlements/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999/ledger
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Settling directly
###
### Normally Invoice calls this when a payment is confirmed. Calling it twice
### for the same invoice returns 200 with the existing settlement rather than
### 201, and does NOT credit the merchant again.
###
### That idempotency is not politeness, it is what makes the retry safe. Invoice
### retries this call by design, so a duplicate arrival is expected traffic. The
### unique index on (invoice_id, entry_type) enforces it in the database, which
### matters because an application-level check can race with itself under
### concurrent requests and a unique index cannot.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{settlement}}/api/settlements
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invoiceId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "merchantId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "amountZar": 250.00,
  "reference": "MANUAL-SETTLE-001",
  "asset": "BTC"
}

### Send it again. 200, not 201, and the balance does not move.
POST {{settlement}}/api/settlements
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invoiceId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "merchantId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "amountZar": 250.00,
  "reference": "MANUAL-SETTLE-001",
  "asset": "BTC"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Webhook delivery: the retry pattern
###
### The delivery log shows attempt counts climbing and the next scheduled
### attempt. The seeded merchant points at http://localhost:9999, which is
### deliberately unreachable inside the container, so deliveries fail and retry:
###
###   attempt 1 -> next in ~3s
###   attempt 2 -> next in ~6s
###   attempt 3 -> next in ~13s
###   attempt 4 -> next in ~25s
###   attempt 5 -> next in ~45s   (capped)
###   attempt 6 -> Failed, dead-lettered, CRITICAL event raised
###
### The jitter matters more than it looks. Without it, a hundred deliveries that
### failed together would retry together for ever, arriving as synchronised
### bursts that are themselves a small denial of service.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{gw}}/api/settlements/webhooks?merchantId={{merchantId}}
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Only the dead letters.
GET {{gw}}/api/settlements/webhooks?merchantId={{merchantId}}&status=Failed
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### Requeue one after the merchant has fixed their endpoint. 202.
### Resets the schedule, not the history.
POST {{gw}}/api/settlements/webhooks/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/retry
X-API-Key: {{key}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Showing a delivery SUCCEED, and the signature being verified
###
### /demo/webhook-sink is a test receiver standing in for a merchant's server.
### It is a harness, not part of the product, and it does what a real
### integration should: recompute the HMAC over timestamp + "." + raw body,
### compare in fixed time, and reject anything older than five minutes.
###
### Point the merchant's webhook at it, then pay an invoice.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1. Log in for a dashboard token.
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@democoffee.co.za", "password": "demo-password-123" }

### 2. Repoint the webhook. Note this raises MERCHANT_WEBHOOK_URL_CHANGED,
###    because repointing where payment notifications go is a classic account
###    takeover step.
###    Inside the compose network the sink is http://gateway:8080/demo/webhook-sink.
PUT {{gw}}/api/merchants/{{merchantId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

{ "webhookUrl": "http://gateway:8080/demo/webhook-sink" }

### 3. Create and pay an invoice, then look at what arrived. Expect
###    "verdict": "verified" on attempt 1.
GET {{gw}}/demo/webhook-sink

### Clear the sink between demo runs.
DELETE {{gw}}/demo/webhook-sink

### Put the webhook back to the broken URL to demonstrate retries again.
PUT {{gw}}/api/merchants/{{merchantId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

{ "webhookUrl": "http://localhost:9999/webhooks/pandapocket" }

### Health, and the OpenAPI document.
GET {{settlement}}/health

###
GET {{settlement}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
